   "title": "Bombardier, CRJ900 Airport Planning Manual (CSP C-020, Revision 11), 00-02-02 Dimensions (aircraft 15036 on): Table 1, Table 3, Figure 4 Aircraft Dimensions (sheets 1-2), Figure 6 Door Dimensions and Clearances",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off Figure 4's side, plan and front views for aircraft 15036-15037, 15040-15041 and 15043 on (tools/trace/crj9/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. The side view is drawn at the static ground angle and was turned level; the front view is drawn 1.353 times larger than the side and was rendered to its scale. The CRJ700's traced points (CRJ7) moved by its two fuselage plugs, then snapped onto this sheet; the longer wing, its winglet, the tail and nacelle re-placed here. The side view draws the 24 cabin windows a side, the passenger door, the two overwing exits and the three cargo doors, all on the left (Figure 6). The right side's service door is placed as on the CRJ700 (Figure 6's dashed outline: the same door); the optional aft service door on the right is left out. The aft cargo door's top is behind the nacelle in the drawing: its height is Table 3's 0.84 m. The engine's position is Detail A's (2.29 m out, as the CRJ700's). All checks within 0.6%."
  }
